kscreenlocker 6.7.5: rearm fingerprint PAM after fprintd becomes device-ready.

After suspend/resume, pam_fprintd can return PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL and the greeter
latches m_unavailable for its lifetime (nixpkgs#432276). Instead of killing
kscreenlocker_greet, recreate the fingerprint PAM handle once GetDefaultDevice
returns a path, then tryUnlock again.

Also only cancel authenticators on prepareForSleep(true); resume triggers rearm.

